## Overview
We collect about 1,800 million events per day from our web and mobile apps, stream them through Kinesis and Firehose, and land them in an S3 data lake. A nightly EMR job cleans the raw data into curated tables, which load into Redshift for analysts to query through Looker.

## Architecture diagram
diagram lake dir=LR title="Clickstream pipeline"
lake: apps "Web and Mobile Apps" user
lake: stream "Clickstream Stream" queue "Kinesis"
lake: firehose "Firehose" svc
lake: raw "Raw Bucket" store
lake: curated "Curated Bucket" store
lake: glue "Glue Catalog" db
lake: emr "EMR Cluster" svc focus
lake: redshift "Redshift Cluster" db "4 x ra3.4xlarge" focus
lake: looker "Looker" ext
lake: apps -> stream : events
lake: stream -> firehose : batch
lake: firehose -> raw : parquet every 5 min
lake: raw -> emr : nightly ETL
lake: emr -> curated : cleaned tables
lake: curated -> redshift : COPY
lake: glue -> emr : schemas
lake: redshift -> looker : SQL
lake: group ingest "Ingest account" stream, firehose
lake: group lakevpc "Lake VPC 10.40.0.0/16" emr, redshift
lake: group analytics "Analytics account" raw, curated, glue, lakevpc

